# Operator functions

Named function forms of the built-in operators, for passing to higher-order routines (map,
filter, reduce). Pure LOGOS over the native operators; identical on every tier. Auto-imported on
reference.

## Note
Returns `x + y`, the function form of integer addition.

## To opAdd (x: Int, y: Int) -> Int:
    Return x + y.

## Note
Returns `x - y`, the function form of integer subtraction.

## To opSub (x: Int, y: Int) -> Int:
    Return x - y.

## Note
Returns `x * y`, the function form of integer multiplication.

## To opMul (x: Int, y: Int) -> Int:
    Return x * y.

## Note
Returns `x / y`, integer (floor) division.

## To opFloorDiv (x: Int, y: Int) -> Int:
    Return x / y.

## Note
Returns `x mod y`, the integer remainder.

## To opMod (x: Int, y: Int) -> Int:
    Return x mod y.

## Note
Returns `0 - x`, the arithmetic negation of `x`.

## To opNeg (x: Int) -> Int:
    Return 0 - x.

## Note
Returns the absolute value of `x`: negates it when negative, otherwise returns `x` unchanged.

## To opAbs (x: Int) -> Int:
    If x is less than 0:
        Return 0 - x.
    Return x.

## Note
Returns `x & y`, the bitwise AND of two integers.

## To opAnd (x: Int, y: Int) -> Int:
    Return x & y.

## Note
Returns `x | y`, the bitwise OR of two integers.

## To opOr (x: Int, y: Int) -> Int:
    Return x | y.

## Note
Returns `x xor y`, the bitwise exclusive-OR of two integers.

## To opXor (x: Int, y: Int) -> Int:
    Return x xor y.

## Note
Returns `x` shifted left by `y` bits.

## To opLshift (x: Int, y: Int) -> Int:
    Return x shifted left by y.

## Note
Returns `x` shifted right by `y` bits.

## To opRshift (x: Int, y: Int) -> Int:
    Return x shifted right by y.

## Note
Returns true when `x` is less than `y`, otherwise false.

## To opLt (x: Int, y: Int) -> Bool:
    If x is less than y:
        Return true.
    Return false.

## Note
Returns true when `x` is less than or equal to `y` (false only when `x` is greater than `y`).

## To opLe (x: Int, y: Int) -> Bool:
    If x is greater than y:
        Return false.
    Return true.

## Note
Returns true when `x` is greater than `y`, otherwise false.

## To opGt (x: Int, y: Int) -> Bool:
    If x is greater than y:
        Return true.
    Return false.

## Note
Returns true when `x` is greater than or equal to `y` (false only when `x` is less than `y`).

## To opGe (x: Int, y: Int) -> Bool:
    If x is less than y:
        Return false.
    Return true.

## Note
Returns true when `x` is equal to `y`, otherwise false.

## To opEq (x: Int, y: Int) -> Bool:
    If x is equal to y:
        Return true.
    Return false.

## Note
Returns true when `x` is not equal to `y` (false only when they are equal).

## To opNe (x: Int, y: Int) -> Bool:
    If x is equal to y:
        Return false.
    Return true.

## Note
Returns the logical negation of `x`: false when `x` is true, otherwise true.

## To opNot (x: Bool) -> Bool:
    If x is equal to true:
        Return false.
    Return true.

## Note
Returns the boolean `x` unchanged, its truthiness.

## To opTruth (x: Bool) -> Bool:
    Return x.

## Note
Returns `x` unchanged, the unary-plus identity.

## To opPos (x: Int) -> Int:
    Return x.

## Note
Returns the bitwise NOT of `x`, computed as `(0 - x) - 1` (the two's-complement `~x`).

## To opInvert (x: Int) -> Int:
    Return (0 - x) - 1.

## Note
Returns `a / b`, floating-point (true) division of two Reals.

## To opTrueDiv (a: Real) and (b: Real) -> Real:
    Return a / b.
